WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.140
Wheel of Fortune Family Edition, the exciting software version of television's number one game show has an all new Family Edition.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:34.820
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.220
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:45.280
And when I say every, you know I mean it when I have us play the third iteration of the same Wheel of Fortune game.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.460
We do these pretty often.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:55.280
Yeah, between Wheel of Fortune, Jeopardy, and I mean all the other game show games basically all function the same and have the same kind of notes for the NES version.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.220
So there's not much ground to cover here on Wheel of Fortune Family Edition.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:12.160
In case you didn't know, it's basically the things that the puzzles that you solve are now more oriented for the whole family versus the championship edition that came before it.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:18.140
Which, to be honest, didn't really feel any different than the regular version of Wheel of Fortune.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.340
And to be honest, a family edition doesn't feel that different.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.460
It just feels like you're paying.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.700
Yeah, this one doesn't feel any different either.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.900
Yeah, you're just paying for puzzles.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.020
You're just saying like, hey, I finished every single puzzle in the other Wheel of Fortune, so give me this one.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.880
You know what they should do?

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.620
They should do a puzzle designer.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.820
For, like, for Wheel of Fortune.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.040
Yeah, yeah. So, like, you could put the letters where you want them.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.660
Okay. It would be awesome.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.160
Great. Yeah, and actually, I just want to get everybody on the same page.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.200
I said championship edition, but it was junior edition.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.440
Jeopardy has a championship edition.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.340
My bad. I mean, tomato, tomato.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.480
No, I am really bad for not knowing that.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.820
That's like, if there's one thing you have to know about Wheel of Fortune, it's the three versions that Rare released.

